 "text": "4 workouts a week feels like failing if you plan 7. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us, reason 18. We plan for a perfect week, 7 runs. Then real life, a late meeting, a cold, a birthday, 4 out of 7. 4 runs is good but next to 7 it's 57%, a fail every week so you quit. So count the runs you actually did in the last 2 weeks, that's your plan. Did 4, plan 4, hit it 2 weeks in a row, add 1. Same 4 runs now 100%, a week you want to repeat. Send this to the friend who plans 7 and quits in week 2. That's what demure is for, archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, this afternoon why staying up late for your gold backfires. How many days did you really manage last week, the links in the bio.",
